course: dictionary
lesson: 1372
title: Reading the clues in a place word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A canyon is a deep, narrow valley with steep rocky sides. You may not know the word, but the words around it give you clues. «The Colorado River carved the Grand Canyon, about 1.8 km deep, over roughly the last 5-6 million years.» A river carving something means cutting into it, and "1.8 km deep" tells you the canyon goes down a long way. Put your meaning into the sentence to check it fits.
explain: Look for the clue words. «Valles Marineris is a canyon system about 4,000 kilometres long and up to 7 kilometres deep.» Long and deep are the clues here. A canyon is a valley, but it is much deeper and narrower than a normal valley, with rock walls on each side.
explain: Stories use canyons as places for adventure. «The Wollemi pine was found in a hidden canyon near Sydney in 1994.» Hidden tells you the canyon is hard to find, so it is a place where something secret could survive. You can use the same method for any new word: find the clues, then check your guess.
fact: A canyon is a deep, narrow valley with steep rocky sides.
fact: Most canyons are cut by a river over a very long time.
fact: The Grand Canyon in Arizona, USA, is the most famous canyon, and it is about 1.8 km deep.
fact: Valles Marineris on Mars is a canyon system about 4,000 km long, which would stretch across Europe.
fact: Canyon walls are the steep rocky sides of a canyon.
exercise: «The Colorado River carved the Grand Canyon over millions of years.» What does a canyon look like? | A small pond in a forest | A tall mountain covered in snow | *A deep, narrow valley with steep rocky sides | A flat, wide plain with no hills
exercise: «A canyon that would stretch across Europe» tells you that a canyon is very big. What does stretch across Europe suggest? | *It is very long | It is full of water | It is made of ice | It is very short
exercise: Which feature do canyons usually have? | Soft sandy beaches | A fountain at the top | Thick grass all the way down | *Steep rocky sides
test: «The Wollemi pine was found in a hidden canyon near Sydney in 1994.» What does hidden suggest about the canyon? | A canyon made of glass | A canyon that is shallow and wide | *A canyon that is hard to find | A canyon in the middle of a busy city
test: Which canyon is the most famous one in the lessons? | Sydney's hidden canyon | *The Grand Canyon in Arizona, USA | Valles Marineris on Mars | Olympus Mons
exam: What does canyon mean in «the Grand Canyon, about 1.8 km deep»? | *A deep, narrow valley with steep rocky sides | A wide, flat field of grass | A cave under the sea | A tall, pointed mountain
